@@ -9202,3 +9202,4 @@ Did NOT modify research-roadmap.yaml or scripts/research_conductor.py. Did NOT p
 - 2026-06-16: Operational retrospective for milestone 2026.06.396 (results/operational_retro_2026_06_396.json, schema carnot.operational_retro.v64). The milestone-scoped timing detector again reported 0 experiments / 0 wall-time / 0 compute-bound — the SAME recurring false-zero artifact documented across .363-.395, now extending to .396. Per the anti-hallucination guard the retro's locked numeric fields stay 0/0/null; the interpretive fields diagnose the recurring detector gap (observability, not execution) as the milestone's only operational bottleneck. GPU-idle correctly NOT flagged: both RTX 3090s idle at the snapshot (0% util, 4MB each) but 0 compute-bound tasks present, so gpu_idle_on_compute_bound_tasks=null per the GPU-idle interpretation rule. On-disk ground truth (the ops/changelog.md window read this turn + results/experiment_4281..4289_*.json) shows the milestone in fact ran exp4281-exp4289 and returned an HONEST NEGATIVE on its headline question (did the EXTERNAL energy verifier IMPROVE generation, not just rank it?): the learned verifier CANNOT score partial/masked denoising states, so the DiffusionGemma guidance-moat arm BLOCKED (exp4281 complete_diffusiongemma_learned_verifier_cannot_score_partial_states, guidance_moat_holds=false); the ARC-GEN 2nd-substrate cross-family hardening was EXCLUDED as flagged_adversarial (exp4282 → capstone arcgen_excluded_flagged), so cross-family-hardens-on-ARC-GEN is unconfirmed this milestone. OFFSETTING WINS: the owed north-star §5 EFFICIENCY axis LANDED — exp4284 efficiency_parity_at_lower_cost=true (the energy verifier matches LLM-as-judge selection accuracy, delta 0.4423, at <=0.1x cost); ARC accuracy advanced +1 to 21 total levels (exp4285 new game ls20-9607627b → L1); self-learning came back a POWERED honest-negative (exp4283 powered_static_is_the_ceiling_for_self_learning). Infra slots clean — SOTA ingestion (exp4286 v397 mapped), registry/gaps hygiene (exp4287 regression_guard_passed=True, 1 gap logged), hardware continuity (exp4288: PolarFire hash-verified CPU dispatch OK, GateMate blocked/unreachable, KV260 terminal). Capstone exp4289 diffusiongemma_thesis_state=partial_state_blocked; 1 flagged-skipped (exp4282). Top operational fix: repair the milestone-scoped timing detector (commit-to-milestone attribution) + add an on-disk results/ mtime fallback + a detector_gap_suspected tripwire, and gate the retro on experiments_completed>=1. estimated_time_savings_pct=0 (no wall-time data to optimize). Appended research-log narrative entry. Did NOT modify docs/roadmap.md, docs/index.html, README.md, scripts/research_conductor.py, or research-roadmap.yaml.
 - 2026-06-16: Archive .396 -> activate .397; KEEP the hardened green-gate + poison-test quarantine. Assert research-complete.yaml + ops/exclusion_manifest.yaml parse under yaml.safe_load; run the smart-subset pre-test gate green; RECORD the .396 close-state truthfully: EFFICIENCY = a clean oracle-distinct PARETO WIN (exp4284 energy 0.654 vs Qwen3.6-35B judge 0.212, delta CI95 [0.308,0.577] excludes 0, cost_ratio 1.95e-08, verifier_is_oracle=false) but the judge scored below random so it needs hardening; DiffusionGemma guidance BLOCKED (exp4281 cannot_score_partial_states); cross-GENERATOR STILL OPEN (exp4282 FLAGGED degenerate -- wrong-majority-only pool + 4 candidates, the within-pool win exp4271 +0.40 STANDS); self-learning powered-static-ceiling but tier-2 was a no-op bug (exp4283 FLAGGED tautology); ARC +1 to 21 (exp4285 ls20); paper_ready=True (FoVer 0.9131, G1-G4). Frame .397 as CLOSE-the-cross-GENERATOR-axis + UNBLOCK-the-in-generation-thesis (partial-state scorer) + HARDEN-the-efficiency-Pareto-win. (⚠️ Blocked) — honest_verdict=success: archived_v396_v397_active_efficiency_pareto_True_partial_state_blocked_True_cross_generator_open_True_arc21_pretest_green; results/experiment_4290_archive_v396_activate_v397.json
 - 2026-06-16: PHASE A1 (THE HEADLINE; P0 oracle-distinct frontier) -- CLOSE the cross-GENERATOR axis with a NON-degenerate ARC-GEN pool. .395 proved the oracle-distinct verifier-beats-vote win generalizes across families CARVED FROM ONE POOL (exp4271 +0.40 held-out, leak-free, 5-seed). The .396 ARC-GEN 2nd-substrate attempt (exp4282) was FLAGGED DEGENERATE: the pool was wrong-majority-only (vote@1=0.0 structural) with 4 candidates/task (correct trivially separable -> set_encoder@1=1.0), giving a meaningless +1.0 CI[1.0,1.0] that measures pool degeneracy, NOT cross-generator transfer (audit: docs/research-notes/exp4282-arcgen-degenerate-audit-2026-06-16.md). The cross-GENERATOR axis -- whether the verifier transfers to a CONSTRUCTION-DISJOINT generator -- is the LAST open axis of the selection moat. REBUILD a NON-degenerate ARC-GEN pool (arXiv:2511.00162, github.com/google/ARC-GEN; gitignore the clone): realistic candidate counts (NOT wrong-majority-only -- include tasks where vote CAN win), report vote@1 well above 0 and an oracle ceiling BELOW 1.0 (headroom the verifier must EARN). Train the set-encoder on train-generators; test beats-vote on HELD-OUT generators. Report per-substrate lift SEPARATELY (original-ARC / ARC-TGI / ARC-GEN). Emit cross_generator_holds BARE bool := (held-out ARC-GEN delta>0 AND CI95-excl-0 AND vote_at_1>0.05 AND oracle_at_k<1.0 AND delta<0.95 -- the non-degenerate guards). verifier_is_oracle=false. HARD-CAP to the window; an honest partial pool (>=5 generators, >=~12 held-out tasks/fold) is fine. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: arcgen_cross_generator_generalizes; results/experiment_4291_arcgen_cross_generator_nondegenerate.json
+- 2026-06-16: PHASE B1 (UNBLOCK the §5 in-generation thesis; harness-first BUILD) -- build + GATE a learned PARTIAL-STATE diffusion scorer for DiffusionGemma masked canvases, with a LEAK audit. .396 (exp4281) BLOCKED the in-generation moat with honest_verdict cannot_score_partial_states: no learned Carnot verifier can score PARTIAL (masked) DiffusionGemma denoising states. Standard PRMs are 'brittle or ill-calibrated' on masked states because they assume a left-to-right prefix (Prism, arXiv:2602.01842). BUILD the missing capability: a small learned value head over masked canvases (Manta-LM 2605.14531 closed-loop control template) that exposes score_partial_state(canvas, step) -> energy, trained on final exact-grid outcomes via the llama.cpp PR binary (~/.cache/llama.cpp-master/build/bin/llama-diffusion-gemma-eval). CRITICAL harness-first deliverable: a PASSING test that the scorer scores partial states NON-DEGENERATELY on a HELD-OUT fixture (partial_state_auroc > 0.6 on held-out canvases) -- NOT the full guidance run (that is exp4293, gated on this). CRITICAL leak audit: if partial-target labels LEAK the final answer (the scorer just reads the canvas's revealed cells = the answer), the rerun is CIRCULAR not a learned external moat -- emit partial_state_leak_free BARE bool from a leak ablation (mask the answer-bearing cells; if the scorer still scores, it is leak-free). verifier_is_oracle=false. NO TRM training; an honest partial_state_scorer_built=false (cannot build a non-degenerate, leak-free scorer) is COMPLETE and gates exp4293 off. (⚠️ Research Finding) — honest_verdict=complete: partial_state_diffusion_scorer_built_leak_free; results/experiment_4292_partial_state_diffusion_scorer_build.json
